{%- comment -%}
  The one block a merchant adds to their product page. Replaces the three
  separate blocks this app used to ship (Build a Box, Fixed Bundle, Quantity
  Breaks) — they all lived in the same spot on the same template, and picking
  the wrong one for the bundle you'd built was the easiest mistake to make.
  Which widget a product gets is decided here instead, from the product's own
  data. Mix & Match keeps its own block: it's placed deliberately, configured
  with a pasted Bundle ID, and isn't a product-page hero widget.

  Precedence, and why:
  1. Build a box, 2. Fixed — these two can never collide. Each publishes its
     own parent product, so a product carries at most one of the two
     metafields. The order between them is arbitrary and never exercised.
  3. Quantity breaks — only when neither bundle metafield is present. A
     Quantity Breaks bundle scoped to "All products" DOES match bundle parent
     products, so without this gate a bundle page would show both widgets.
     Skipping it here also saves the app-proxy round trip below on every
     bundle page.

  Nothing is editable from the theme editor: every option lives in the Magyx
  Bundle admin, which is why there are no schema settings. The block
  self-hides on products that have no bundle at all.

  The schema's "javascript" key is a tiny loader — Shopify's app-block JS size
  check (10KB) only scans that declared file, so each widget's real
  implementation is loaded at runtime from the `data-magyx-impl-src` the
  matching branch below emits, and isn't subject to that check.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign slot_data = product.metafields.magyx_bundle.slot_builder.value -%}
{%- assign fixed_data = product.metafields.magyx_bundle.components.value -%}

{%- render 'magyx-custom-css' -%}

<div class="magyx-bundle-widget" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
  {%- if slot_data.bundleId != blank -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Pool contents aren't in the metafield (a collection-scoped pool can
      change without a republish) — the widget's JS fetches those live from
      the app proxy instead.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div
      class="magyx-slot-builder"
      style="--bc-accent: {{ slot_data.settings.accentColor | default: '#1a1a1a' }};"
      data-money-format="{{ shop.money_format | escape }}"
      data-locale="{{ request.locale.iso_code | escape }}"
      data-magyx-impl-src="{{ 'magyx-bundle-slot-builder-impl.js' | asset_url }}"
    >
      <script type="application/json" data-magyx-slot-builder-data>
        {{ slot_data | json }}
      </script>
      <div class="magyx-slot-builder__state"></div>
    </div>

  {%- elsif fixed_data != blank -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Assigned first: `render` parameters take a value, not a filtered
      expression. `default_variant_id` is passed rather than read off the
      global `product` inside the snippet — `render` gives the snippet an
      isolated scope, so being explicit about what it depends on beats
      relying on what happens to be global at the call site.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign fixed_impl_src = 'magyx-bundle-fixed.js' | asset_url -%}
    {%- render 'magyx-bundle-contents',
      bundle_data: fixed_data,
      impl_src: fixed_impl_src,
      default_variant_id: product.variants.first.id
    -%}

  {%- else -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      The only widget with no server-side gate: whether a Quantity Breaks
      bundle covers this product depends on scope (ALL / PRODUCTS /
      COLLECTIONS), and collection membership needs a live lookup. So the
      container always renders on non-bundle products and its JS asks the app
      proxy, self-hiding when nothing applies.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div
      class="magyx-quantity-breaks"
      data-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
      data-money-format="{{ shop.money_format | escape }}"
      data-magyx-impl-src="{{ 'magyx-bundle-quantity-breaks.js' | asset_url }}"
    >
      <div class="magyx-quantity-breaks__state"></div>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Magyx Bundle",
  "target": "section",
  "stylesheet": "magyx-bundle.css",
  "javascript": "magyx-bundle-loader.js",
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
